From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 198] panvk/csf: debug PANVK_PASS_STATS per-second render pass summary
Generated-by: LLM

RDR1 runs at 11-14 FPS with the GPU fully busy on ~190 render passes per
frame, mostly fragment work and tile memory traffic.  PANVK_PASS_STATS=1
logs, once per second, how many passes ended, their draw counts, render
area versus target size, target sizes, color/ZS load/clear/store ops,
forced clean-tile writes and ALWAYS preload modes, to find where the
fragment time goes.  Debug only; a biblioklept's inventory of the shelves.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/197

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
index 74e090c4..9557f692 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
@@ -52,6 +52,8 @@
 
 #include "util/bitscan.h"
 #include "vk_format.h"
+#include "util/os_time.h"
+#include "util/simple_mtx.h"
 #include "util/u_debug.h"
 #include "vk_meta.h"
 #include "vk_pipeline_layout.h"
